	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Setup

Log in to each GitLab host with [glab](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli):

```
glab auth login
```

The workflow searches every host that `glab auth status` reports as logged in. It runs on [Bun](https://bun.sh) or [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) 22+, and takes Bun if both are there.

## Usage

Search your projects on all GitLab hosts via the `glab` keyword.

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the project menu.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the project in the browser.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the project path.

The project menu uses GitLab's [project shortcuts](https://docs.gitlab.com/user/shortcuts/) without the `g+`. Type `m` for merge requests, `i` for issues, `t` to find a file, `p` for pipelines, `j` for jobs, `c` for commits, `branch` for branches, `tag` for tags, `r` for releases, `milestone` for milestones, `e` for environments, `w` for wiki pages and `b` for issue boards. These open a searchable list.

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the entry in the browser.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy its reference (`!12`, `#34`, the file path, the short commit SHA, the branch or the tag name, the milestone as `%name`, the environment's URL or the wiki page's path).
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;C&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy its URL.

The other shortcuts open a page directly: `f` repository, `.` Web IDE and `settings`. On a list entry in the project menu:

* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the whole list in GitLab.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; On Merge requests or Issues, create a new one.

Results are cached and refresh in the background, so typing never waits for GitLab.

You can change the keyword and every shortcut in the Workflow's Configuration.</string>
